            <ArticleTitle>Left and right coronary artery to left ventricular fistula: demonstration of myocardial ischemia by treadmill test and Holter monitoring--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>977-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fistulous communication from the coronary artery to the left ventricle is extremely rare. The authors report such a case in a sixty-year-old woman with chest pain. They demonstrated myocardial ischemia on treadmill test and Holter monitoring in this patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
